sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    title HackMatch — US-032: Private Direct Messaging — Sequence Diagram
    actor PART as Verified Active PART
    participant UI as React DM UI
    participant API as Express API, Guards + Service
    participant DB as PostgreSQL / Supabase

    PART->>UI: Open Direct messages
    UI->>API: Request inbox
    API->>API: Require session, MFA, active verified PART
    alt Caller is ineligible
        API-->>UI: 401 or generic 403 without private content
    else Caller is eligible
        API->>DB: Find pair threads ordered by recent activity
        DB-->>API: Threads and latest messages
        API-->>UI: Safely projected inbox or empty list
    end
    UI-->>PART: Render inbox, empty, denied, or error state

    opt Open or continue a conversation
        PART->>UI: Choose an eligible participant
        UI->>API: Submit participant identifier
        API->>API: Reject self, ineligible peer, or either-direction block
        API->>DB: Find or create sorted low/high participant pair
        Note right of DB: Unique pair makes A–B and B–A one thread
        DB-->>API: Existing or newly created thread
        API-->>UI: Safe thread projection
    end

    PART->>UI: Select an inbox thread
    UI->>UI: Clear stale messages and show loading
    UI->>API: Request persisted thread and messages
    API->>DB: Resolve thread and verify caller is in its pair
    alt Missing thread or unrelated caller
        DB-->>API: No authorized thread
        API-->>UI: Generic 403 without querying messages
    else Caller belongs to thread
        API->>DB: Load messages oldest first
        DB-->>API: Messages or empty list
        API-->>UI: Allowlisted handle, fromMe, UTC time, and body
    end
    UI-->>PART: Render thread, empty, denied, or error state

    PART->>UI: Submit message draft
    UI->>UI: Validate nonblank body and 4,000-character limit
    alt Validation fails
        UI-->>PART: Show error and retain draft
    else Validation passes
        UI->>API: Submit message to selected thread
        API->>DB: Recheck pair membership, peer eligibility, and blocks
        alt Access changed or either participant blocked the other
            DB-->>API: Denied
            API-->>UI: Safe 403 without private-state details
            UI-->>PART: Show denial and retain draft
        else Send authorized
            API->>DB: Insert message
            Note right of DB: Trigger enforces author in pair and updates last_message_at
            DB-->>API: Created message
            API-->>UI: Safely projected created message
            UI-->>PART: Append once and clear draft after success
        end
    end

    Note over API,DB: US-030 public forums and US-031 team chat remain separate models and authorization paths.

